    "result_text": "The repository contains a single test class (`AcceptanceTest`), and it passes along with the full `mvn test` build.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented rejection of owner creation with **400 Bad Request** when the email domain is on the disposable-domain blocklist (`mailinator.com`, `tempmail.com`, `guerrillamail.com`).\n\nChanges, following the existing validation idioms in the codebase:\n\n1. **New exception** `rest/advice/DisposableEmailDomainException.java` \u2014 a `RuntimeException` carrying the rejected email, mirroring `InvalidPostcodeException`.\n\n2. **`OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`** \u2014 added a `validateEmailDomain(owner.getEmail())` call in the create flow (right after telephone normalization), plus a `DISPOSABLE_EMAIL_DOMAINS` constant and a `validateEmailDomain` helper. Email is optional, so null/blank or no-`@` values pass through; the domain is compared case-insensitively (the stored email is already lower-cased) against the blocklist and throws when matched.\n\n3. **`ExceptionControllerAdvice`** \u2014 added an `@ExceptionHandler` for `DisposableEmailDomainException` returning 400 with the `errors` array naming the `email` field, consistent with the other field-level handlers.\n\n`Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 **BUILD SUCCESS**.",
